      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If opening the `packed-refs` file fails with `FileNotFoundeException` doesn\u0027t that proof that the file doesn\u0027t exist and hence we should return `false` here ?\n\nNot unconditionally.\n\n- `FileNotFoundException` means the open failed; it does not always prove the path is absent.\n- If `packed-refs` was previously loaded and is then deleted, returning `false` would retain stale packed refs. Returning `true` lets `readPackedRefs()` replace them with `NO_PACKED_REFS` ([RefDirectory.java:1057](https://github.com/eclipse-jgit/jgit/blob/bf0f0ad1cc2ce422604383272a4a4b8b3947b465/org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/internal/storage/file/RefDirectory.java#L1057), [RefDirectory.java:1081](https://github.com/eclipse-jgit/jgit/blob/bf0f0ad1cc2ce422604383272a4a4b8b3947b465/org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/internal/storage/file/RefDirectory.java#L1081)).\n\n\u003e Otherwise repos not having `packed-refs` (only loose refs) do an unnecessary refresh\n\nThe loose-only refresh concern is real, but it is pre-existing: `NO_PACKED_REFS.shouldRefresh()` always returns `true` ([RefDirectory.java:1580](https://github.com/eclipse-jgit/jgit/blob/bf0f0ad1cc2ce422604383272a4a4b8b3947b465/org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/internal/storage/file/RefDirectory.java#L1580)). Changing this catch would not fix that path.\n\nA correct optimization would require retaining a “missing file” snapshot and returning false only while the file remains absent, while still detecting its later creation.",
